  "conclusion": "The faithful casmi port differs from nanoGPT long-axis adaptation and paper RMS scaling. A genuine cached-state restore bug exists, but the prior replay compensates and fresh training does not load optimizer checkpoints. Changing the adaptation axis did not rescue either the failed local replay or fresh HalfCheetah 8M seed-1 training: final-100-episode means were Adam 8,281, row adaptation 5,873, and long-axis adaptation 5,907. This does not establish universal optimizer inferiority or uniquely identify the internal cause.",
